<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niklaus von Flüe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1417">1417</a>–<a href="/years/1487">1487</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Brother Klaus, Bruder Klaus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niklaus von Flüe was a Swiss farmer, soldier and magistrate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obwalden">Obwalden</a> who left his family in 1467 to live as a hermit in the Ranft gorge. His advice, sent to the Diet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stans">Stans</a> in December 1481, helped the cantons reach the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stans-agreement">Stans Agreement</a> and avoid civil war. He was canonised in 1947 and is venerated as the patron saint of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niklaus-von-flue.jpg" alt="Niklaus von Flüe" width="250" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Geogre on en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicholas-Flue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
